Species with blue or violaceous tints
2,0 $ Almost unicolorous dark-violaceous or blackish-violet discolouring blackish-brown with sl.  violaceous tinge (flesh sl. paler in part and gills becoming rusty-bay or purplish umber);  cap entirely velvety-scaly; spores large, ± amygdaliform, 11-15/7-9 µm ; facial and marginal  ± lageniform or fusiform-cylindric cystidia present $ violaceus (131)
2,3 $ Not so; (if ± unicolorous blue-violaceous, spores smaller and facial and marginal cystidia  absent)
