11,12 $ Gills lemon, chrome or olive-yellow then rusty-ochre or olive-rusty; cap olive- or lemonyellow  to reddish-brown or chestnut-umber, ± fibrillose-tomentose at least around  margin, rarely conical but sometimes acutely umbonate
11,0 $ Gills pale or golden-yellow then tawny-ochre or rusty-buff; cap tawny-brick or tawnybuff  with darker disc and yellower margin, almost smooth, often ± conical; (stem yellow  with paler apex then tawny-ochre or rusty from base up; spores 7½-9½(10)/4½-5½(6) µm ,  elliptic (Fig. 17) $ croceoconus (154)
